        ]
      },
      "predicate": "STRUCTURAL_REGION",
      "value": "CANCEL_PUSH frame carries a push ID encoded as a variable-length integer. The Push ID field identifies the server push that is being cancelled; see Section 4.6.",
      "state": "RESOLVED",
      "evidenceNeeds": []
    },
    {
      "subject": {
        "sourceParts": [
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1005:S0"
          },
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1006:S0"
          }
        ]
      },
      "predicate": "STRUCTURAL_REGION",
      "value": "If a CANCEL_PUSH frame is received that references a push ID greater than currently allowed on the connection, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_ID_ERROR.",
      "state": "RESOLVED",
      "evidenceNeeds": []
    },
    {
      "subject": {
        "sourceParts": [
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1007:S0"
          },
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1008:S0"
          },
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1009:S0"
          },
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1010:S0"
          }
        ]
      },
      "predicate": "STRUCTURAL_REGION",
      "value": "If the client receives a CANCEL_PUSH frame, that frame might identify a push ID that has not yet been mentioned by a PUSH_PROMISE frame due to reordering. If a server receives a CANCEL_PUSH frame for a push ID that has not yet been mentioned by a PUSH_PROMISE frame, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_ID_ERROR.",
      "state": "RESOLVED",
      "evidenceNeeds": []
    },
    {
      "subject": {
        "sourceParts": [
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1011:S0"
          }
        ]
      },
      "predicate": "STRUCTURAL_REGION",
      "value": "7.2.4. SETTINGS",
      "state": "RESOLVED",
      "evidenceNeeds": []
    },
    {
      "subject": {
        "sourceParts": [
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1012:S0"
          },
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1013:S0"
          },
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1014:S0"
          },
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1015:S0"
          }
        ]
      },
      "predicate": "STRUCTURAL_REGION",
      "value": "The SETTINGS frame (type=0x04) conveys configuration parameters that affect how endpoints communicate, such as preferences and constraints on peer behavior. Individually, a SETTINGS parameter can also be referred to as a \"setting\"; the identifier and value of each setting parameter can be referred to as a \"setting identifier\" and a \"setting value\".",
      "state": "RESOLVED",
      "evidenceNeeds": []
    },
    {
      "subject": {
        "sourceParts": [
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1016:S0"
          }
        ]
      },
      "predicate": "STRUCTURAL_REGION",
      "value": "SETTINGS frames always apply to an entire HTTP/3 connection, never a single stream.",
      "state": "RESOLVED",
      "evidenceNeeds": []
    },
    {
      "subject": {
        "sourceParts": [
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1017:S0"
          },
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1018:S0"
          },
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1019:S0"
          },
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1020:S0"
          }
        ]
      },
      "predicate": "STRUCTURAL_REGION",
      "value": "SETTINGS frame MUST be sent as the first frame of each control stream (see Section 6.2.1) by each peer, and it MUST NOT be sent subsequently. If an endpoint receives a second SETTINGS frame on the control stream, the endpoint MUST respond with a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "state": "RESOLVED",
      "evidenceNeeds": []
    },
    {
      "subject": {
        "sourceParts": [
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1021:S0"
          },
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1022:S0"
          },
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1023:S0"
          }
        ]
      },
      "predicate": "STRUCTURAL_REGION",
      "value": "SETTINGS frames MUST NOT be sent on any stream other than the control stream. If an endpoint receives a SETTINGS frame on a different stream, the endpoint MUST respond with a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "state": "RESOLVED",
      "evidenceNeeds": []
    },
    {
      "subject": {
        "sourceParts": [
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1026:S0"
          },
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1027:S0"
          },
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1028:S0"
          },
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1029:S0"
          },
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1030:S0"
          }
        ]
      },
      "predicate": "STRUCTURAL_REGION",
      "value": "SETTINGS parameters are not negotiated; they describe characteristics of the sending peer that can be used by the receiving peer. However, a negotiation can be implied by the use of SETTINGS: each peer uses SETTINGS to advertise a set of supported values. The definition of the setting would describe how each peer combines the two sets to conclude which choice will be used. SETTINGS does not provide a mechanism to identify when the choice takes effect.",
      "state": "RESOLVED",
      "evidenceNeeds": []
    },
    {
      "subject": {
        "sourceParts": [
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1031:S0"
          },
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1032:S0"
          },
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1033:S0"
          }
        ]
      },
      "predicate": "STRUCTURAL_REGION",
      "value": "Different values for the same parameter can be advertised by each peer. For example, a client might be willing to consume a very large response field section, while servers are more cautious about request size.",
      "state": "RESOLVED",
      "evidenceNeeds": []
    },
    {
      "subject": {
        "sourceParts": [
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1034:S0"
          },
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1035:S0"
          },
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1036:S0"
          }
        ]
      },
      "predicate": "STRUCTURAL_REGION",
      "value": "The same setting identifier MUST NOT occur more than once in the SETTINGS frame. A receiver MAY treat the presence of duplicate setting identifiers as a connection error of type H3_SETTINGS_ERROR.",
      "state": "RESOLVED",
      "evidenceNeeds": []
    },
    {
      "subject": {
        "sourceParts": [
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1037:S0"
          },
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1038:S0"
          }
        ]
      },
      "predicate": "STRUCTURAL_REGION",
      "value": "The payload of a SETTINGS frame consists of zero or more parameters. Each parameter consists of a setting identifier and a value, both encoded as QUIC variable-length integers.",
      "state": "RESOLVED",
      "evidenceNeeds": []
    },
    {
      "subject": {
        "sourceParts": [
          {
            "sourceAlias": "L1048:S0"
          }
        ]
      },
      "predicate": "DOCUMENT_IDENTITY",
      "value": "SRC-095",
      "state": "RESOLVED",
      "evidenceNeeds": []
    },
    {
      "subject": {
        "sourceParts": [
